35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Only two firms are bidding, and they both warned about clay slippage. The south can be hoarded, but the center cannot.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The counts show people stick to hard ground. Drainage callouts have doubled since the culvert was capped.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,The staff roll is down to seven. But two volunteer groups are already active on weekends.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The old basin is fine, but the civic hall apron has been patched three times. Half the avenue trees died.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The habitat fund only pays for planting and water. Upkeep for planted ground is triple the cost of hard surfaces.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the drainage is failing, does that mean we can't do heavy earthworks in the center?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, exactly. The ground is saturated. We need a plan that works with the water, not against it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, if the trees died before, is a woodland plan risky?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, it is risky if we ignore the aftercare. But the basin held up, so water management can work.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the fund terms are strict. We can't build a plaza or courts with this money.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,The slippage risk makes large structures dangerous. We need something light on the ground.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The heat readings are high. We need shade, but not from trees that might die without proper care.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,The volunteers can help with habitat tasks. That fits with a natural plan.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,The planting record is a warning. We must ensure the contract includes watering and maintenance.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"The upkeep cost for water and plants is high, but the fund covers the capital. We must budget for the triple cost.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I am leaning towards a plan that minimizes deep digging.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. The drainage data is the strongest signal we have.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,I feel safer with the volunteer support for a natural area.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I am convinced that water management is the key, provided we learn from the past failures.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I can accept the high upkeep if the capital is fully funded by the habitat grant.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
